---
# Home page (SPEC §6, §7.2, §8.1, §20 M1b; HANDOFF §6.1, §6.3; boards
# Main.dc.html, Landing-Phone.dc.html, Problems-A.dc.html and
# Problems-Phone.dc.html, with the changes in SPEC §7.5). Home is also the
# Sleep problems page (project lead, 2026-11-13): the hero, then the list of
# sleep problems with its filter, then the trial band and the disclaimer.
# The copy below can be edited here; keep values that start with "[" in
# quotes.
#
# Analytics: Home sends no page_view (SPEC §10.2) and the filter sends
# nothing (§8.1), so there is no track_page_view here.
layout: layouts/home.njk
page_id: home
# The browser tab title only: Home shows no title band, and its H1 is
# hero.heading below.
title: Sleep during and after cancer
styles: ["pages/home.css", "pages/problems.css"]
# problems.js: the list's filter and its area buttons (SPEC §7.2, §8.1).
scripts: ["problems.js"]
# The hero subline under the H1; also the page's meta description.
summary: Short videos and practical ideas for the sleep problems people often have during and after cancer. Watch, listen or read, whichever suits you.
hero:
  eyebrow: Free · Short videos · At your own pace
  heading: Sleep can be hard after cancer. It can also get better.
  # Until there is a photo, the arched frame shows this placeholder text.
  photo_text: "[Photo: someone at home in warm evening light, not looking at the camera]"
  # To show a photo, put it in src/img/ and give its file name here, e.g.
  # photo: "home-hero.jpg". It is decorative (alt=""), so choose mood
  # imagery: the H1 carries the message.
  photo: ""
# The Sleep problems section, under the hero. `lede_tools` describes the
# filter and the area buttons, which need JavaScript, so it shows only once
# problems.js has shown them; `lede` is true either way.
sleep_problems:
  eyebrow: Sleep problems
  heading: What's keeping you up?
  lede_tools: Open an area to see its topics, or search in your own words.
  lede: Choose as many as sound like you.
# The "About the trial" band. Drafted from the trial's concept note (version
# 0.3, July 2026) for the team to confirm (SPEC §22).
trial_text: "We're testing this program in a research trial run by a team at Monash University. The trial is for adults with cancer who have trouble sleeping. It tests whether this self-help program helps people sleep better, and whether extra help from a therapist, then a sleep specialist, helps those who need more. You don't need to be in the trial to use this website."
---
{%- from "partials/icons.njk" import icon -%}
{%- from "partials/problem-list.njk" import problemList -%}
{%- set topicAreas = collections.problems | groupByArea(areas) -%}

<section class="home-hero on-dark">
  <div class="home-hero__inner container">
    <div class="home-hero__text">
      <p class="eyebrow home-hero__eyebrow">{{ hero.eyebrow }}</p>
      <h1 class="home-hero__title">{{ hero.heading }}</h1>
      <p class="home-hero__lede">{{ summary }}</p>
      <div class="home-hero__actions">
        <a class="button button--light" href="/start/">{{ icon('play', 16, 'button__icon') }}Start with the introduction</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="home-hero__photo" aria-hidden="true">
      {%- if hero.photo %}
      <img class="home-hero__img" src="/img/{{ hero.photo }}" alt="">
      {%- else %}
      <span class="home-hero__photo-text">{{ hero.photo_text }}</span>
      {%- endif %}
    </div>
  </div>
  {% include "partials/arc.njk" %}
</section>

{#-
  Sleep problems: what the Sleep problems page held until 2026-11-13, on
  the page's paper ground (SPEC §7.2, §7.5). Links elsewhere point here as
  /#sleep-problems, and to an area as /#<area_id>.

  Without JavaScript (SPEC §2, §11) every area is open under a plain
  heading, and the toolbar (the filter) and the lede's sentence about it
  carry `hidden`, so no dead control is ever shown or described; the result
  line ("36 topics in 10 areas") stays, because it is true either way.
  src/js/problems.js shows the toolbar and runs the filter.
#}
<section class="problems-section container" id="sleep-problems" aria-labelledby="sleep-problems-title">
  <p class="eyebrow problems-section__eyebrow">{{ sleep_problems.eyebrow }}</p>
  <h2 class="section-heading" id="sleep-problems-title">{{ sleep_problems.heading }}</h2>
  <p class="problems-section__lede"><span data-problems-hint hidden>{{ sleep_problems.lede_tools }} </span>{{ sleep_problems.lede }}</p>
  {#- Shown by problems.js once its handlers are attached. No <form> and no
      name: nothing is submitted, stored or sent (SPEC §8.1).
      autocomplete="off" keeps typed health terms out of the browser's form
      history and stops a stale value being restored. #}
  <div class="problems-tools" data-problems-tools hidden>
    {#- Not "Search…": that is the header's site search ("Search this
        website"), which leaves the page. This field only narrows the list
        here. #}
    <label class="problems-search__label" for="problem-filter">Find a sleep problem on this page</label>
    <input class="problems-search__input" id="problem-filter" type="search" placeholder="Try: night sweats, 3am, partner" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" aria-describedby="problem-filter-status" data-problem-filter>
  </div>
  <p class="problems-status" id="problem-filter-status" aria-live="polite" data-filter-status>{{ collections.problems.length }} topics in {{ topicAreas.length }} areas</p>
  {{ problemList(topicAreas, keywords) }}
</section>

<div class="home-trial">
  <div class="home-trial__inner container">
    <section class="home-trial__main">
      <p class="eyebrow home-trial__eyebrow">About the trial</p>
      <h2 class="section-heading home-trial__heading">Part of a research study</h2>
      <p>{{ trial_text }}</p>
      <p class="home-trial__link link-standalone"><a href="/about/">More about us and the trial</a></p>
    </section>
    <section class="home-help">
      <h2 class="home-help__heading">Need more help?</h2>
      <p>When to talk to your doctor, and how to see a sleep specialist.</p>
      <p class="home-help__link link-standalone"><a href="/help/">Referral info</a></p>
    </section>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="home-disclaimer container">
  <p class="panel home-disclaimer__text">These videos and ideas don't replace care from your treating team. If your sleep changes suddenly, or you feel unsafe, talk to your doctor or see <a href="/urgent-help/">Getting urgent help</a>.</p>
</div>
